{#
  The chronology drawn as a band.

  Server-rendered SVG on purpose. The graph needed a layout engine and so needed
  Cytoscape; a band of dated spans does not, and `layoutTimelineBand` has
  already computed every coordinate -- including the y of the axis and of its
  labels, so nothing here does arithmetic on a number the module produced.

  Geometry goes in x/y/width/height attributes; colour comes from classes in
  site.css. No `style=` attribute -- the CSP forbids inline styles, and
  check-invariants.mjs fails the build for one.

  The drawing is `aria-hidden`, and its links are removed from the tab order.
  `role="presentation"` does not propagate to focusable descendants, so before
  this a keyboard user tabbed through fifty links inside an element declared
  decorative and then met the same fifty again in the list below. The list is
  the accessible content; a mouse click on a bar still works.
#}
{% if band %}
  <figure class="timeline-band">
    <figcaption class="visually-hidden">
      A chronology covering {{ band.rangeLabel }}, drawn as {{ band.spans.length }}
      {{ 'span' if band.spans.length == 1 else 'spans' }}.
      The list that follows carries the same events.
    </figcaption>

    <svg
      class="band"
      viewBox="{{ band.viewBox }}"
      width="100%"
      height="{{ band.height }}"
      aria-hidden="true"
      focusable="false"
      preserveAspectRatio="none"
    >
      {% for tick in band.ticks %}
        <line class="band-tick" x1="{{ tick.x }}" y1="{{ band.tickY }}" x2="{{ tick.x }}" y2="{{ band.axisY }}" />
        <text
          class="band-tick-label{% if loop.first %} band-tick-label-first{% endif %}{% if loop.last %} band-tick-label-last{% endif %}"
          x="{{ tick.x }}"
          y="{{ band.labelY }}"
        >
          {{ tick.label }}
        </text>
      {% endfor %}

      {#
        Three marks, three meanings. A bar's width is how long the event lasted
        and nothing else: a width that meant "known only to the year" would
        assert a duration the record does not carry. An uncertain span is the
        window an event could have fallen in, so it is outlined rather than
        filled -- a reader must not mistake a bounded guess for a dated fact.
      #}
      {% for span in band.spans %}
        <a href="{{ span.href }}" tabindex="-1">
          <title>{{ span.dateLabel }} — {{ span.title }}</title>
          <rect
            class="band-span{% if span.point %} band-span-point{% endif %}{% if span.uncertain %} band-span-uncertain{% endif %}{% if span.visibility != 'public' %} band-span-private{% endif %}"
            x="{{ span.x }}"
            y="{{ span.y }}"
            width="{{ span.width }}"
            height="{{ band.spanHeight }}"
            rx="3"
          />
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </svg>

    {#
      The figcaption is visually hidden, so without this a sighted reader has no
      way to learn that a dashed outline means something different from a bar.
    #}
    <ul class="band-legend">
      <li><span class="band-key band-key-period"></span>A recorded period</li>
      <li><span class="band-key band-key-point"></span>A single date, at the precision known</li>
      <li><span class="band-key band-key-uncertain"></span>A window between other events</li>
    </ul>

    {% if band.overflow > 0 %}
      <p class="muted small">
        {{ band.overflow }} further
        {{ 'event is' if band.overflow == 1 else 'events are' }}
        listed below but did not fit on the band.
      </p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if band.undated > 0 %}
      <p class="muted small">
        {{ band.undated }} undated
        {{ 'event is' if band.undated == 1 else 'events are' }}
        listed below but cannot be placed on the band.
      </p>
    {% endif %}
  </figure>
{% endif %}
